WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:01.690
A ring of grey rock in the

2
00:00:01.690 --> 00:00:04.372
Andaman Sea, about a hundred and thirty-eight

3
00:00:04.372 --> 00:00:06.717
kilometres from Port Blair.

4
00:00:06.717 --> 00:00:08.398
This is Barren Island.

5
00:00:08.798 --> 00:00:11.166
It is the only confirmed active volcano

6
00:00:11.166 --> 00:00:13.210
in the Indian subcontinent,

7
00:00:13.210 --> 00:00:15.056
and the only live one on a

8
00:00:15.056 --> 00:00:18.897
chain of volcanoes from Sumatra to Myanmar.

9
00:00:19.297 --> 00:00:21.573
The first recorded eruption came in seventeen

10
00:00:21.573 --> 00:00:22.803
eighty-seven.

11
00:00:22.803 --> 00:00:25.681
Travellers sketched the smoking cone soon after.

12
00:00:26.081 --> 00:00:28.461
Then, after a few more eruptions,

13
00:00:28.461 --> 00:00:30.086
it went quiet for nearly a hundred

14
00:00:30.086 --> 00:00:31.758
and fifty years.

15
00:00:31.758 --> 00:00:33.918
Geologists still came to survey it and

16
00:00:33.918 --> 00:00:34.926
draw it.

17
00:00:35.326 --> 00:00:37.555
In nineteen ninety-one it woke again,

18
00:00:37.555 --> 00:00:40.016
and that eruption lasted six months.

19
00:00:40.016 --> 00:00:41.537
More eruptions followed,

20
00:00:41.537 --> 00:00:43.567
some seen from space.

21
00:00:43.967 --> 00:00:46.417
So the record runs from seventeen eighty-seven,

22
00:00:46.417 --> 00:00:47.926
through a long sleep,

23
00:00:47.926 --> 00:00:50.629
to repeated eruptions in our own time.

24
00:00:51.029 --> 00:00:52.608
For Prelims, remember:

25
00:00:52.608 --> 00:00:54.837
Barren Island, in the Andaman Sea,

26
00:00:54.837 --> 00:00:57.552
is India's only confirmed active volcano.

